<mrow>\begin{pmatrix}
\leading1 \amp 0 \amp 0 \\
0 \amp \leading1 \amp 0 \\
0 \amp 0 \amp \leading1
\end{pmatrix}</mrow>
</md>,the <m>3\times 3</m> identity matrix.  So by <xref provisional="theorem-?"/> the original matrix is nonsingular and its columns are therefore a linearly independent set.</p>
